{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-03 finite-pass fuse threshold research (pending maintainer decision). Correction: an absolute five-failures-per-pass cap is unsafe for large healthy batches because five isolated failures among hundreds of successes would falsely open the provider. Maintained controllers usually requeue per entity; established circuit-breaker mechanics instead combine consecutive failures with sliding-window density. Envoy defaults to five consecutive raw 5xx responses; Resilience4j uses a 50% failure-rate threshold over a configurable window/minimum. Because one Rebar exhausted logical outcome already represents up to three physical calls, recommendation is: inferred endpoint-family scope opens after 3 consecutive exhausted provider-suspect logical outcomes across at least 2 tickets, or 5 exhausted among the latest 10 eligible outcomes after the window fills, across at least 2 tickets. Provider scope uses the same 3-consecutive or 5-of-10 thresholds but additionally requires at least 2 independent endpoint families. A matching success resets only the consecutive counter and remains in the rolling window; isolated old failures age out. Count only exhausted timeout/connect/unknown-429/5xx outcomes and actual provider successes; exclude permanent 4xx, validation, conflict, per-issue throttling, local deferral, and skipped calls. Authoritative auth/config/TLS/global/burst/per-issue/DC-rate signals keep their already-approved immediate scopes. Continuous outage therefore stops after at most 9 physical calls/45s retry sleep; alternating failure/success opens at 50% after 10 eligible operations. Fuse state is pass-local; retry_not_before carries deferral. Detailed note: .joe-janitor/rp03-jira-failure-taxonomy.md. No tracked files or RP-04 state changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787015844130548001,"uuid":"875b6042-4415-4351-b781-150cea6fc468"}